PicoEFI
=======

PicoEFI is a minimal build environment for EFI applications written in C, with
headers compatible with C and C++.

It provides the EFI headers, and, for each supported architecture, the entry
stub, self-relocator, and linker script needed to build an EFI application as a
position-independent ELF executable that is then converted into a PE image.

Supported architectures: x86_64, ia32, aarch64, arm, riscv64, riscv32,
loongarch64, and loongarch32.

On IA-32, programs must be built with -malign-double: UEFI aligns 64-bit fields
to 8 bytes, which the IA-32 ABI does only with that flag. The headers check for
it when built as C11 or C++11 and later.

For an example on how to use this, see:
https://github.com/PicoEFI/picoefi-c-template
